			"notes": "First release of MetalCraft: Minecraft Java Edition 26.2 rendered with Apple Metal on Apple Silicon Macs.\n\n**Experimental.** Tested on one machine (MacBook Pro M1 Max) with Fabric Loader 0.20.1, Fabric API 0.161.0+26.2 and Fabric Language Kotlin 1.14.2. The jar was run from the development environment; it has not been tried in a separate launcher installation yet.\n\n## What is in it\n\n- A Metal renderer for the game (no OpenGL while it is in use)\n- A shader pack engine that runs packs converted to Metal, with the packs' own option screens\n- MetalFX upscaling (spatial and temporal)\n- Create Fly 6.0.9: Flywheel instancing on Metal, lit by the shader pack\n- Zoom key, player and entity shadows in shader packs\n\n## Files\n\n- `MetalCraft-0.1.0.jar`: the mod. Put it into `mods`.\n- `metalcraft-porter.jar`: the shader pack converter. No shader packs are included; convert your own copy:\n  `java -XstartOnFirstThread -jar metalcraft-porter.jar \"<pack>.zip\" \"<game folder>/shaderpacks/<name>\"`\n\n## Shader packs tested\n\nComplementary Reimagined r5.9.3, Sildur's Vibrant 2.02, Solas 3.9, Photon 1.4, AstraLex 93.0 and Kappa 5.3 work. Bliss 2.1.2 works by day; its night and Nether colours are wrong. Rethinking Voxels does not work (compute and geometry shaders are not implemented).\n\nSee the README for frame rates and the list of known limitations. 한국어 설명은 README.ko.md에 있습니다."
		}
